      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When it comes to syncing, this is not a good solution. It introduces magic strings and magic formatting & parsing for json in an attempt to extend json for something it is not made for. Note that using json as an intermediate step for syncing is already a workaround (even if it's recommended), so adding a bandaid to a workaround is in general not a good idea. It tends to add more edge cases and complexity.\n\nIf I were to suggest/request a change when it comes to syncing DataLists and DataDictionaries (and DataTokens in the process), it would be a request for native syncing support for those data types. That way they could be serialized to much more space optimized binary data and handle both the issues you've mentioned, plus several other cases. Considering the docs mention that using json is the \"current\" recommended method for syncing, I feel like there's a chance for native syncing support.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
